@Test
void lastReadingRacingReleaseIsConsistent() throws Exception {
    long programId = createProgram("GLAZE-K", 1);
    long batchId = createBatch("B-RACE-1", programId);
    // 缺少终点边界点
    int[][] partial = Arrays.copyOf(fullTrajectory(), 8);
    upload(batchId, "req-race-0", partial).andExpect(status().isOk());

    CountDownLatch ready = new CountDownLatch(2);
    CountDownLatch start = new CountDownLatch(1);
    ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(2);
    Future<String> uploadFuture = pool.submit(() -> {
        ready.countDown(); start.await(5, SECONDS);
        try {
            readingService.upload(batchId, "req-race-1",
                List.of(new ReadingService.ReadingInput(T0.plus(40, MINUTES), new BigDecimal("800"))));
            return "UPLOAD_OK";
        } catch (ApiException e) { return "UPLOAD_" + e.status().value(); }
    });
    Future<String> releaseFuture = pool.submit(() -> {
        ready.countDown(); start.await(5, SECONDS);
        try {
            releaseService.release(batchId, "qc-wang");
            return "RELEASE_OK";
        } catch (ApiException e) { return "RELEASE_" + e.status().value(); }
    });
    ready.await(5, SECONDS); start.countDown();
    String uploadResult = uploadFuture.get(15, SECONDS);
    String releaseResult = releaseFuture.get(15, SECONDS);
    pool.shutdownNow();

    if (releaseResult.equals("RELEASE_OK")) {
        // 放行必须包含最后一个测温点：不存在未审点
        assertEquals("UPLOAD_OK", uploadResult);
        var release = releaseRepository.findByBatch(batchId).orElseThrow();
        Long maxId = readingRepository.maxIdByBatch(batchId);
        assertEquals(maxId, release.readingMaxId());
        assertEquals(9, release.readingCount());
    } else {
        // 按旧上限明确拒绝：缺少终点边界，批次仍未放行，补录点已入库，可复检通过
        assertEquals("RELEASE_422", releaseResult);
        assertEquals("UPLOAD_OK", uploadResult);
        assertEquals(0, releaseRepository.countByBatch(batchId));
        releaseService.release(batchId, "qc-wang"); // 重新检查通过
        assertEquals(1, releaseRepository.countByBatch(batchId));
    }
}
```

Wait — is there an outcome where upload gets 409 and release OK? Upload 409 happens if batch already RELEASED when upload runs. But release can only succeed if the end-boundary point exists, which only the upload provides. So if release succeeded, upload committed first → upload OK. If upload got 409, release succeeded without the point — impossible since validation would fail. So the assertion `assertEquals("UPLOAD_OK", uploadResult)` when RELEASE_OK is correct. And UPLOAD_409 implies release succeeded first — impossible as argued. Actually could upload get 409 while release failed? No: upload 409 requires status != FIRING, i.e., release committed. Then release OK. But release OK requires the point... contradiction → UPLOAD_409 can't happen. Fine.

Edge: H2 FOR UPDATE — reading upload and release both lock the batch row. Good.

One concern: H2's SELECT ... FOR UPDATE with MVStore — supported.

Also note the "同参重放" test expects `X-Idempotent-Replay: false` header on first upload. OK.

